<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; \old(this.get(i)) == this.get(i));</code>

However, the comment specifies that the element at a position should either be null if it was originally null or remain unchanged. This means we need to account for the possibility that the element could have been null initially. Here's the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (\old(this.get(i)) == null || \old(this.get(i)) == this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i) == null);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
